<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Champa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Champa was a group of kingdoms of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> people on the central and southern coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, from the early centuries CE until absorbed by Vietnam. It was a maritime trading power linked to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Fast-ripening <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> varieties from Champa transformed agriculture under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/champa.jpg" alt="Champa" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laska666 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Linyi_and_Chamic_states_of_the_fifth_century_AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
